cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AI-Aquatica: Reproducible Machine Learning and Hydrochemical Analysis of Water-Quality Data"
message: "If you use AI-Aquatica in your research, please cite this software release."
type: software
version: "2.3.0"
license: "MIT"

authors:
  - family-names: "Miller"
    given-names: "Tymoteusz I."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2514-5583"

keywords:
  - "water quality"
  - "hydrochemistry"
  - "machine learning"
  - "environmental monitoring"
  - "reproducible research"

abstract: >-
  AI-Aquatica is an open-source Python library for reproducible
  water-quality and hydrochemical analysis. It integrates hydrochemical
  quality control, leakage-safe machine-learning workflows, grouped
  validation, visualization, and self-contained reporting.
